Strategy            unique_key   idempotent on re-run
  append               no          NO -- duplicates, every time
  merge                yes         yes
  delete+insert        yes         yes
  insert_overwrite     no          yes -- replaces whole partitions
  microbatch           no          yes -- one bounded batch per slice

Producer defaults in Kafka 4.x (idempotence is ON):
  enable.idempotence                     true

The consume-transform-produce loop, atomic across output AND offsets:

  producer.initTransactions();
  while (true) {
    records = consumer.poll(d);
    producer.beginTransaction();
    for (r : records) producer.send(transform(r));
    producer.sendOffsetsToTransaction(offsets, consumer.groupMetadata());
    producer.commitTransaction();   // output + offsets, together
  }

Consumers of the output MUST set isolation.level = read_committed.
The default is read_uncommitted.

@dag(schedule="@daily", catchup=False, max_active_runs=1,
     start_date=pendulum.datetime(2026, 1, 1, tz="UTC"),
     default_args={"retries": 3})
def rollup():
    @task
    def load(data_interval_start=None, data_interval_end=None):
        # run of 2026-03-01: start=03-01T00:00, end=03-02T00:00, and the
        # task BEGINS at 03-02T00:00, once the interval has closed
        return f"WHERE ts >= '{data_interval_start}' AND ts < '{data_interval_end}'"
    load()

# logical_date == data_interval_start: the START of the period processed,
# not the moment the task runs.
